\v 13 There they¦86117 produced the false¦86120 witnesses¦86119 saying¦86123, “This¦86128 man¦86127 won't¦86129 stop spreading messages¦86134 against this¦86141 holy¦86140 \add temple\add* and¦86142 against the¦86143 law¦86144
\v 14 because¦86146 we¦86145 heard¦86145 him¦86147 saying¦86148 that that \nd Yeshua¦86150\nd* from¦86152 \nd Nazareth¦86152\nd* will be tearing¦86154 down¦86154 this¦86157 building and¦86158 will be changing¦86159 the¦86160 traditions that Mosheh¦86166 gave¦86164 to¦86165 us¦86165.”
\v 15 So¦86167 then¦86167 the¦86180 council¦86181 members looked¦86168 across at¦86171 Stephen and¦86167 saw¦86183 that his¦86186 face¦86185 \add was shining\add* like that of one \add of God's\add* messengers¦86189.
\c 7
\s1 Stephen's history discourse and accusations
