\p
\v 1 Then¦86195 the¦86196 chief¦86197 priest¦86197 asked \add Stephen\add*, “Is¦86205 all this true?”
\p
\v 2 And¦86207 he replied, “My brothers¦86211 and¦86207 fathers¦86213, please listen¦86214. Our¦86222 honoured \nd God¦86216\nd* was¦86208 seen¦86219 by¦86220 our¦86222 ancestor Abraham¦86223 in¦86225 Mesopotamia¦86227 before¦86228 he moved to¦86230 Haran¦86233\x + \xo 7:2-3: \xt Gen 12:1.\x*
\v 3 and he¦86235 told him¦86237, ‘Leave your land¦86242 and your relatives¦86247, and go to¦86257 the¦86252 place that I will¦86258 show¦86258 you¦86257.’
\v 4 So¦86269 he left Chaldea¦86264 and moved to Haran¦86268, and then¦86269 after¦86272 his¦86277 father¦86276 died¦86274, he moved again to this¦86284 land¦86283 where we now¦86288 live.\x + \xo 7:4: a \xt Gen 11:31; \xo b \xt Gen 12:4.\x*
\v 5 Abraham hadn't received any land here as an¦86301 inheritance¦86301, in¦86302 fact he'd never been near this land and nor¦86304 did he have any children¦86328, yet God promised¦86309 to give¦86311 this \add entire\add* country to him¦86312 and his¦86321 descendants¦86320.\x + \xo 7:5: \xt Gen 12:7; 13:15; 15:18; 17:8.\x*
\v 6 And¦86347 yet \nd God¦86334\nd* \add also\add* told him¦86342 that¦86337 his¦86342 descendants¦86340 would end up staying in¦86344 another¦86346 country where they¦86348 would be¦86348 enslaved¦86348 and¦86351 mistreated¦86352 for four¦86355 hundred¦86355 years¦86354.\x + \xo 7:6-7: \xt Gen 15:13-14.\x*
\v 7 However \nd God¦86369\nd* promised to punish the¦86357 nation¦86359 that enslaved them, and told him that in the end they¦86363 would leave that place¦86381 and serve¦86363 him here in this¦86382 country¦86359.\x + \xo 7:7: \xt Exo 3:12.\x*
\v 8 And¦86383 he contracted with Abraham about¦86387 being circumcised, and so¦86389 when Abraham had Isaac, he circumcised him¦86395 on the¦86398 eighth¦86400 day¦86397, and then¦86383 Isaac went on to have Yacob, and Yacob to have the \add twelve\add* tribal leaders.\x + \xo 7:8: a \xt Gen 17:10-14; \xo b \xt Gen 21:2-4; \xo c \xt Gen 25:26; \xo d \xt Gen 29:31–35:18.\x*
\p
\v 9 Those brothers went on to become jealous¦86415 of¦86417 Yosef¦86417 and¦86412 sent him back¦86418 into¦86419 Egypt¦86420 \add as a slave\add*, but¦86412 \nd God¦86424\nd* was¦86422 with¦86425 him\x + \xo 7:9: a \xt Gen 37:11; \xo b \xt Gen 37:28; \xo c \xt Gen 39:2,21.\x*
\v 10 and rescued¦86428 him out¦86430 of all his¦86434 troubles there. Then God gave¦86436 him wisdom¦86441 and caused him to¦86437 gain the favour¦86438 of \add Far'oh (Pharaoh)\add*, the king¦86445 of Egypt, who then appointed¦86448 him as the ruler of all Egypt and over¦86451 Far'oh's¦86444 own household¦86457.\x + \xo 7:10: \xt Gen 41:39-41.\x*
\v 11 Then¦86461 a famine¦86462 hit all¦86464 Egypt¦86470 and Canaan¦86472 causing great¦86475 distress and our¦86482 ancestors¦86481 were¦86478 unable to find¦86478 enough food¦86479.\x + \xo 7:11: \xt Gen 42:1-2.\x*
\v 12 But¦86485 Yacob¦86486 heard¦86483 that grain¦86488 was available in¦86490 Egypt¦86492, so first¦86501, he sent¦86494 off our¦86500 tribal leaders.
\v 13 On¦86504 their second¦86506 visit, Yosef revealed himself to¦86518 them, and¦86513 so Far'oh¦86518 became¦86515 aware of¦86512 Yosef's¦86509 heritage.\x + \xo 7:13: a \xt Gen 45:1; \xo b \xt Gen 45:16.\x*
\v 14 Then¦86525 Yosef¦86526 sent¦86524 for his¦86531 father¦86530 Yacob¦86528 and¦86533 all¦86534 the¦86535 extended family—some seventy-five¦86540 of¦86531 them.\x + \xo 7:14: a \xt Gen 45:9-10,17-18; \xo b \xt Gen 46:27 (LXX).\x*
\v 15 So¦86544 Yacob¦86547 went¦86545 to Egypt¦86549, where he¦86552 and¦86544 the¦86555 \add twelve\add* tribal leaders eventually died¦86551,\x + \xo 7:15: a \xt Gen 46:1-7; \xo b \xt Gen 49:33.\x*
\v 16 although their bodies were moved to¦86561 Shekem¦86562 where they¦86564 were put¦86564 into the¦86566 tomb¦86567 that¦86569 Abraham¦86571 had bought from¦86574 the¦86575 sons¦86576 of¦86577 Hamor¦86577.\x + \xo 7:16: \xt Gen 23:3-16; 33:19; 50:7-13; Josh 24:32.\x*
\p
\v 17 But¦86602 as¦86583 the¦86586 time¦86588 limit promised¦86593 to¦86598 Abraham¦86598 by \nd God¦86596\nd* was¦86585 getting closer, \add our\add* people¦86601 multiplied¦86603 in¦86604 Egypt¦86605\x + \xo 7:17-18: \xt Exo 1:7-8.\x*
\v 18 until¦86606 another¦86610 Far'oh \add !(Pharaoh)\add* ended up¦86608 ruling there who¦86613 had¦86616 never known¦86616 Yosef¦86619.
\v 19 He took¦86623 advantage¦86623 of¦86624 us¦86626 Jews and mistreated¦86627 our¦86626 ancestors¦86629, even forcing them¦86637 apart from their¦86637 own babies¦86635 so they wouldn't live.\x + \xo 7:19: a \xt Exo 1:10-11; \xo b \xt Exo 1:22.\x*
\v 20 Mosheh¦86647 was¦86646 born¦86646 during that¦86653 time¦86644 and¦86648 \nd God¦86652\nd* considered him beautiful¦86650. He¦86649 spent three¦86656 months¦86655 in¦86657 his \add own\add* father's¦86661 house¦86659\x + \xo 7:20: \xt Exo 2:2.\x*
\v 21 before being placed outside¦86665, from where Far'oh's¦86676 daughter¦86675 took¦86672 him and¦86666 brought¦86678 him up¦86678 herself¦86681 as her own son¦86683.\x + \xo 7:21: \xt Exo 2:3-10.\x*
\v 22 So¦86684 Mosheh¦86686 was instructed¦86685 in¦86687 all¦86688 the wisdom¦86691 of¦86693 the Egyptians, and was a powerful¦86697 speaker and project leader.
\p
\v 23 But¦86705 when¦86704 he hit forty¦86710, it entered his mind¦86715 to¦86709 visit¦86717 his relatives, the¦86714 Israelis¦86723.\x + \xo 7:23-29: \xt Exo 2:11-15.\x*
\v 24 When¦86724 he noticed one¦86726 of them being¦86727 mistreated, he retaliated¦86731 and while defending the oppressed man¦86726, he struck¦86738 \add and killed\add* the Egyptian.
\v 25 He¦86747 thought¦86747 his¦86759 relatives would understand¦86750 that \nd God¦86756\nd* was¦86747 bringing salvation¦86762 to¦86750 them¦86763 via him¦86759, but¦86766 they¦86764 didn't¦86767 see it that way.
\v 26 So¦86771 on¦86770 the following¦86772 day¦86773 when he saw¦86774 two of them¦86775 quarrelling¦86776, he tried to¦86787 resolve the situation by saying¦86789, ‘Men¦86792, you're all¦86794 brothers¦86793. Why¦86797 are¦86798 you injuring¦86798 each¦86794 other?’
\v 27 But¦86813 the bullying one pushed¦86806 him¦86807 away¦86806 and¦86813 said¦86808, ‘Who¦86809 made you¦86810 the judge¦86814 over¦86815 us¦86817?
\v 28 Do you want¦86822 to¦86819 kill¦86819 me¦86820 like you killed¦86825 that¦86823 Egyptian yesterday¦86826?’
\v 29 When¦86834 he heard that¦86839, Mosheh¦86835 fled¦86833 \add Egypt\add* and¦86834 became¦86841 an exile in¦86843 Midian¦86845 where¦86846 he \add eventually\add* had two¦86849 sons¦86848.\x + \xo 7:29: \xt Exo 18:3-4.\x*
\p
\v 30 After another forty¦86858 years¦86856, he was¦86859 in the¦86862 wilderness¦86863 around Mt¦86865. Sinai¦86867 when he saw¦86859 a messenger¦86868 in the flame¦86871 of¦86865 a burning¦86872 thorn¦86875 bush.\x + \xo 7:30-34: \xt Exo 3:1-10.\x*
\v 31 Mosheh¦86878 was amazed at¦86882 the¦86882 vision¦86883 when he saw¦86879 it¦86889, so he approached¦86885 \add the bush\add* to¦86889 look more closely when he heard Yahweh's voice¦86891 saying,
\v 32 ‘I am¦86900 the god of your¦86905 ancestors¦86904—the god of Abraham¦86908 and of Isaac¦86912 and of Yacob¦86916.’ At that point, Mosheh¦86921 started trembling¦86917 and was¦86924 scared to go any closer to look,
\v 33 but¦86931 \nd Yahweh¦86936\nd* said¦86928, ‘Take off your¦86945 sandals¦86940, because¦86947 the¦86935 ground¦86956 you're standing¦86955 on¦86951 is¦86958 dedicated to¦86934 God.
\v 34 I have noticed¦86962 the¦86963 mistreatment¦86964 of¦86965 my¦86967 people¦86966 in¦86969 Egypt and heard¦86976 their¦86974 groaning¦86973 and so I came¦86979 down¦86979 to rescue¦86980 them¦86981, so now¦86983 I'm going to send¦86985 you¦86987 \add back\add* to Egypt.’
\p
\v 35 This was the same Mosheh¦86992 that they¦86994 had previously rejected and asked who¦86996 had made him ruler and judge¦87001 over them. Now \nd God¦87006\nd* had indeed sent¦87014 him as ruler and liberator by¦87021 means of¦87018 the messenger¦87018 that he saw¦87020 in¦87022 the¦87023 thorn¦87024 bush.\x + \xo 7:35: \xt Exo 2:14.\x*
\v 36 So eventually Mosheh led¦87026 them¦87027 out¦87026 of Egypt¦87036 after doing¦87029 miracles¦87032 and signs¦87032 of God's power there, and then also¦87031 at the Red¦87040 Sea¦87041 and during the forty¦87047 years¦87046 in¦87043 the¦87044 wilderness¦87045.\x + \xo 7:36: a \xt Exo 7:3; \xo b \xt Exo 14:21; \xo c \xt Num 14:33.\x*
\v 37 This¦87057 same Mosheh¦87051 told Israelis¦87056 that in the¦87050 future \nd God¦87062\nd* would raise¦87059 up¦87059 another prophet¦87057 like¦87070 him from¦87065 among them.\x + \xo 7:37: \xt Deu 18:15,18.\x*
\v 38 Now Mosheh was the person that \add led\add* the¦87080 assembly¦87081 \add of people\add* in¦87082 the¦87083 wilderness¦87084, was spoken¦87089 to by one \add of God's\add* messengers¦87087 on Mt¦87093. Sinai¦87094, and¦87095 one of our¦87099 ancestors¦87097 that received¦87102 living¦87105 messages to pass on to us.\x + \xo 7:38: \xt Exo 19:1–20:17; Deu 5:1-33.\x*
\p
\v 39 “Yet our¦87117 ancestors¦87116 didn't¦87111 want to¦87110 obey that man, so they¦87119 rejected him and¦87120 started thinking about¦87117 Egypt¦87133 again,
\v 40 saying¦87134 to Aaron¦87136, ‘Make¦87137 some gods¦87139 for¦87138 us to lead us because¦87144 we've¦87156 got no idea what¦87157 happened to that¦87146 Mosheh¦87145 who¦87140 led¦87150 us out¦87150 of¦87154 Egypt¦87154.’\x + \xo 7:40: \xt Exo 32:1.\x*
\v 41 So¦87161 together they made¦87162 a calf¦87162 as an idol¦87172 to bring¦87168 sacrifices¦87170 to, and¦87161 they were¦87174 pleased with what they'd achieved.\x + \xo 7:41: \xt Exo 32:2-6.\x*
\v 42 But¦87186 \nd God¦87185\nd* turned¦87181 and¦87186 allowed them¦87188 to¦87189 serve¦87189 the¦87192 heavenly¦87193 armies¦87191, just as¦87194 the¦87198 prophets¦87199 wrote¦87195,\x + \xo 7:42-43: \xt Amos 5:25-27 (LXX).\x*
\q1 ‘It¦87195 wasn't me¦87205 that you¦87204 Israelis¦87213 sacrificed¦87203 to for¦87207 those forty¦87207 years¦87206 in¦87208 the¦87209 wilderness¦87210.
