\v 19 But¦95170 when her¦95152 masters¦95151 realised that¦95155 their¦95162 profitable business¦95161 was about¦95152 to come to an end, they¦95173 grabbed¦95167 Paul¦95169 and Silas¦95172 and dragged¦95173 them¦95173 to the authorities at the¦95175 marketplace¦95176.
\v 20 They¦95186 brought¦95181 them¦95183 forward¦95181 to¦95184 face the magistrates and¦95180 said¦95186, “These¦95187 Jews¦95195 are¦95190 disturbing¦95190 \add the peace\add* in our¦95192 city¦95194
\v 21 and¦95197 teaching behaviour that¦95202 we as Romans can neither accept¦95207 nor¦95210 practice¦95211.”
\v 22 An \add angry\add* crowd¦95219 gathered around and the¦95218 magistrates ordered for Paul and Silas to have¦95228 their¦95229 robes¦95231 torn¦95228 off¦95228 and then¦95215 to be¦95233 beaten¦95233 with¦95233 rods¦95233.
\v 23 They¦95240 were severely beaten and¦95236 then¦95236 thrown¦95240 into¦95241 prison¦95242 where the¦95246 officer was commanded¦95243 to¦95249 keep¦95249 them¦95251 secure¦95248.
\v 24 Because of¦95272 that¦95252, he threw¦95260 them¦95261 into¦95262 the¦95263 inner¦95264 cell and¦95266 locked their¦95267 feet¦95268 in¦95273 stocks¦95277.
\p
\v 25 Around midnight¦95282 Paul¦95287 and Silas¦95290 were praying¦95291 and singing¦95292 praises to \nd God¦95294\nd*, and the¦95299 other prisoners¦95301 were listening¦95295 to them¦95297.
\v 26 Suddenly¦95302 there was¦95325 a strong earthquake¦95304 that¦95307 shook¦95308 even the¦95309 foundations¦95310 of the prison, and immediately¦95316 all the prison doors¦95318 opened¦95313 up¦95313 and the¦95322 chains¦95323 of all the prisoners came loose.
\v 27 The¦95330 prison officer woke up¦95334, and¦95328 when he saw¦95333 that all the prison doors¦95336 were open¦95334, he drew¦95341 his sword¦95343 to¦95349 take his own life as he figured that all the¦95350 prisoners¦95351 must have¦95349 escaped¦95349.
\v 28 But¦95353 Paul¦95359 shouted¦95360 out, “Don't harm¦95365 yourself¦95363! We're all¦95366 still here¦95369!”
\p
\v 29 The¦95384 officer called for torches, then¦95372 rushed¦95375 in and knelt down trembling¦95377 in front¦95380 of Paul¦95385 and Silas¦95388.
\v 30 Then¦95389 he escorted them¦95393 out¦95394 and¦95389 asked¦95400, “Masters¦95402, what¦95403 do I need to do to be¦95406 saved¦95408?”
